Chapter: GearsKernel
  cites Gpu chapter DeviceEffect
  cites Gpu chapter DeviceMath

 Rotating meshing gears, rasterized per pixel from Codex [Device] AST. Each gear
 is an implicit shape: a pixel is inside if its radius from the gear centre is
 below the tooth profile (a square wave of the polar angle) and outside the hub
 hole. Three gears of different tooth counts spin at speeds inversely
 proportional to their teeth and in alternating directions, so they mesh. The
 polar angle uses a rational atan2 (no atan2 intrinsic needed). Reference site's
 "gears" technique. Float math from DeviceMath.

 We say:

Section: Parameters

  gr-width : Integer = 1024
  gr-half-h : Integer = 384

Section: Rational atan2

  gr-atan2 : Real, Real -> Real
  gr-atan2 (y) (x) =
    let ax = if x < 0.0 then 0.0 - x else x
    in let ay = if y < 0.0 then 0.0 - y else y
    in let mn = real-min ax ay
    in let mx = real-max ax ay
    in let a = if mx > 0.0 then mn / mx else 0.0
    in let a2 = a * a
    in let base = a * (105.0 + 55.0 * a2) / (105.0 + a2 * (90.0 + 9.0 * a2))
    in let r1 = if ay > ax then 1.5707963 - base else base
    in let r2 = if x < 0.0 then 3.1415926 - r1 else r1
    in if y < 0.0 then 0.0 - r2 else r2

Section: Gear Shape

 Shade contribution of a gear at (cx, cy): returns a lit intensity if the pixel
 is inside the gear body, else -1.

  gr-gear : Real, Real, Real, Real, Real, Real, Real -> Real
  gr-gear (px) (py) (cx) (cy) (teeth) (rtip) (spin) =
    let dx = px - cx
    in let dy = py - cy
    in let r = real-sqrt (dx * dx + dy * dy)
    in if r > rtip then 0.0 - 1.0
    else if r < rtip * 0.22 then 0.0 - 1.0
    else let a = gr-atan2 dy dx + spin
    in let k = real-to-int (a * teeth / 3.1415926 + 2000.0)
    in let toothon = k - (k / 2) * 2
    in let rroot = rtip * 0.80
    in let outer = if toothon == 0 then rtip else rroot
    in if r > outer then 0.0 - 1.0
    else if r < rtip * 0.34 then 0.62
    else if r < rtip * 0.42 then 0.30
    else 0.55 + r / rtip * 0.45

Section: Kernel

  gr-render : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  gr-render (gid) (frame) =
    let px = real-from-int (gid - (gid / gr-width) * gr-width)
    in let py = real-from-int (gid / gr-width)
    in let f = real-from-int frame / 30.0
    in let g0 = gr-gear px py 410.0 384.0 12.0 160.0 f
    in let g1 = gr-gear px py 654.0 300.0 8.0 108.0 (0.0 - f * 1.5)
    in let g2 = gr-gear px py 470.0 156.0 10.0 128.0 (0.0 - f * 1.2)
    in if g2 >= 0.0 then gr-pack g2 0.55 0.72 0.95
    else if g1 >= 0.0 then gr-pack g1 0.95 0.75 0.35
    else if g0 >= 0.0 then gr-pack g0 0.85 0.35 0.30
    else let h = py / 768.0 in gr-pack 1.0 (0.04 + h * 0.04) (0.05 + h * 0.06) (0.09 + h * 0.10)

  gr-pack : Real, Real, Real, Real -> Integer
  gr-pack (lit) (r) (g) (b) =
    let ri = real-to-int (real-min 255.0 (lit * r * 255.0))
    in let gi = real-to-int (real-min 255.0 (lit * g * 255.0))
    in let bi = real-to-int (real-min 255.0 (lit * b * 255.0))
    in ri * 65536 + gi * 256 + bi

Section: Gears Kernel

  gears-step : Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Device] Integer
  gears-step (outb) (frame) (gid) = act
    device-store outb gid (gr-render gid frame)
  end
